From 3ce67f46a3d15e244b7948e1e4afe8c7645820c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikit Hamal <iamnikithamal@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 16:12:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CI: build APKs from any branch, and stop wasting a runner on
 non-app commits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Trigger
- push now matches every branch, but is gated by a paths: filter on
  agent-app/**, customer-app/** and the two workflow files. GitHub evaluates
  paths: before allocating a runner, so a dashboard-only commit no longer
  spends ~20s spinning up detect-changes just to decide there is nothing to do
  — the run is never created.
- workflow_dispatch can now be pointed at any branch from the Actions tab, with
  a build_target (both / customer-app / agent-app) and a publish checkbox.

detect-changes
- Dropped actions/checkout and dorny/paths-filter. Cloning the repo purely to
  diff it was most of this job's runtime; one compare API call returns the same
  file list. Manual runs skip the API entirely.
- Fail-safe: no base sha (new branch/force push), an empty response, or a
  truncated 300-file diff all build both apps rather than silently skipping.
- Removed the old 'workflow' output that OR'd into both build jobs; a workflow
  change now just sets customer=true and agent=true directly.

Publishing
- New publish input on the reusable workflow, defaulting to false. The R2 steps
  (which rewrite latest.json / agent-latest.json and therefore offer the build
  to every installed device) are gated on it.
- publish is true only for pushes to main, or a manual run with the box ticked.
  Branch and PR builds now produce a signed APK/AAB artifact and touch nothing
  in production.
- Added a job summary showing version, package, artifact name and whether the
  build was published.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
